[{'name': 'python_interpreter', 'args': {'code': 'def solve_cube_beads():\n    """\n    The problem asks for the number of ways to color the vertices of a cube with 8 different colors,\n    where rotations are considered the same.\n    This is an application of Burnside\'s Lemma.\n    \n    Burnside\'s Lemma: Number of orbits = (1 / |G|) * sum_{g in G} |X^g|\n    where G is the group of rotations of a cube, and X^g is the set of colorings fixed by rotation g.\n    \n    The group of rotations of a cube (G) has 24 elements:\n    1. Identity rotation (1): Fixes all 8! colorings? No, the colors are different.\n       Wait, the problem says "8 beads of different colors". This means each color is used exactly once.\n       So we are looking for the number of permutations of 8 colors on 8 vertices, modulo the rotation group.\n       \n       Let X be the set of all 8! ways to assign 8 distinct colors to the 8 vertices.\n       The size of X is 8!.\n       For each rotation g in G, we need to find the number of colorings in X that are fixed by g.\n       A coloring is fixed by g if for every vertex v, the color at v is the same as the color at g(v).\n       Since all 8 colors are distinct, a coloring can only be fixed by g if g(v) = v for all v.\n       This only happens for the identity rotation.\n       \n       Wait, let\'s re-read. "8 beads of different colors".\n       If the colors are all distinct, then for any rotation g other than the identity, \n       there is at least one vertex v such that g(v) != v.\n       If g(v) = u with u != v, then for the coloring to be fixed by g, the color at v must be the same as the color at u.\n       But all colors are distinct, so this is impossible.\n       \n       Therefore, |X^g| = 0 for all g != identity.\n       |X^identity| = 8!.\n       \n       Number of ways = (1 / 24) * (8! + 0 + ... + 0) = 8! / 24.\n    """\n    import math\n    \n    eight_factorial = math.factorial(8)\n    rotations_count = 24\n    \n    result = eight_factorial // rotations_count\n    return result\n\nprint(solve_cube_beads())\n'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-887702ca25c8f5ea', 'type': 'tool_call'}]
